01:02:06,760 --> 01:02:15,320
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: These are projections, but they are also based on an actual, well, you also have to balance it out with the actual borrowings

1119
01:02:15,320 --> 01:02:23,160
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: and also as well as the expenditures and the possible revenue that we collect from both the taxes and also the non-tax revenue that we also collect.

1120
01:02:23,160 --> 01:02:27,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Halimbawa po, sir, naibigay nyo na distinguished sponsor yung projection,

1121
01:02:27,100 --> 01:02:28,620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na pababa ng pababa, ano?

1122
01:02:29,000 --> 01:02:32,360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Paano po kaya kung mangyari uli yung nangyari nung makaraang buwan,

1123
01:02:32,460 --> 01:02:35,520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na may mga external shocks na apektohan tayo?

1124
01:02:35,720 --> 01:02:37,440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Will this be adversely affected?

1125
01:02:37,780 --> 01:02:39,640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Your projections will be adversely affected?

1126
01:02:45,320 --> 01:02:50,560
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Yeah, again, this is not entirely a decision that the Department of Finance has to make.

1127
01:02:50,560 --> 01:02:54,560
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: It also involves other agencies like the DBCC,

1128
01:02:55,220 --> 01:02:56,680
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: as well as,

1129
01:02:57,100 --> 01:03:00,840
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: DEV, DEV, NEDA, BSP.

1130
01:03:00,960 --> 01:03:04,800
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: So it's really an interagency assessment.

1131
01:03:05,000 --> 01:03:16,220
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: So if there's a need to really readjust policies insofar as responding to unplanned and unpredicted shocks in the international market,

1132
01:03:16,220 --> 01:03:27,080
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: definitely the DOF will be one among those agencies that will come up with adjusted policy in order to measurably and adequately respond.

1133
01:03:27,100 --> 01:03:29,480
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: to whatever effects to our economy.

1134
01:03:30,060 --> 01:03:35,080
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Should there be any uncertain or untowards incident that may happen in the coming days?

1135
01:03:35,620 --> 01:03:37,660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Chair, Mr. Sponsor.

1136
01:03:37,940 --> 01:03:41,120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ito po, ito, siguradong hindi na ito sa DBCC,

1137
01:03:41,340 --> 01:03:45,420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kontrolado na po ito ng DOF on revenue mobilization.

1138
01:03:45,960 --> 01:03:55,980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano po kaya ang specific tax measures or administrative reforms na idideliver na what will we use to deliver

1139
01:03:55,980 --> 01:03:59,980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: bulk ng mga ina-assume natin ito?

1140
01:04:00,460 --> 01:04:04,740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At paano natin titiyakin na hindi mabibigatan ang ordinaryong manggagawa?

1141
01:04:05,760 --> 01:04:10,180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Of course, aside from yung na-ipresenta na po na pagbenta ng assets,

1142
01:04:10,180 --> 01:04:19,300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: may dalawa po yata ang plano, yung pagbenta ng baknotan kalayaan na geothermal and the atrium of Makati properties.

1143
01:04:19,440 --> 01:04:25,180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Aside from that, in terms of revenue collections, ano po ang plano ng DOF?

1144
01:04:25,980 --> 01:04:26,980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you.

1145
01:04:32,860 --> 01:04:41,580
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Mr. Speaker, there are several items here if the good lady would indulge me in identifying one.

1146
01:04:41,680 --> 01:04:50,460
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: This is actually a progressive tax reform that the Department of Finance would like to propose.

1147
01:04:50,940 --> 01:04:54,340
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: There's also the increase in personal income tax exemption

1148
01:04:54,340 --> 01:05:00,160
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: from 250,000 to 350,000 annually.

1149
01:05:00,400 --> 01:05:10,000
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: This will actually help our income, personal income taxpayers up to 17,500

1150
01:05:10,000 --> 01:05:12,680
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: with their annual savings, Mr. Speaker.

1151
01:05:13,460 --> 01:05:19,980
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: We do also have exemption for the micro and small enterprises or MSNBs.

1152
01:05:19,980 --> 01:05:24,460
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: We would also like to update.

1153
01:05:25,980 --> 01:05:30,180
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: On the, or the lifting.

1154
01:05:44,900 --> 01:05:50,060
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: So, Mr. Speaker, Your Honors, pardon me if I need to itemize, Mr. Speaker,

1155
01:05:50,360 --> 01:05:53,460
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: some of the tax reform packages that we have.

1156
01:05:53,460 --> 01:05:55,860
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Without going through, what would be?

1157
01:05:55,980 --> 01:06:00,020
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: The direct beneficiary or benefits it will give to our tax payers.

1158
01:06:00,120 --> 01:06:04,060
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: I just want to enumerate to you these tax reform packages.

1159
01:06:05,420 --> 01:06:09,900
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Number one is through the automobiles, e-cigarettes and novel tobacco,

1160
01:06:10,120 --> 01:06:13,580
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: plastics, sweetened beverages, distilled spirits, and vermouth,

1161
01:06:13,660 --> 01:06:20,900
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: which actually with a total revenue impact of 43.62 billion pesos, Mr. Speaker.

1162
01:06:20,900 --> 01:06:24,580
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: So, this would actually give benefit, direct benefit to our tax payers.

1163
01:06:25,180 --> 01:06:26,600
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Mr. Speaker, Your Honors.

1164
01:06:26,600 --> 01:06:36,390
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But that, would that be enough, Mr. Speaker, to, to cover yung malaki pong kakulangan natin sa revenues?

1165
01:06:36,390 --> 01:06:42,680
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Mr. Speaker, the reason why there's a policy to reform our tax packages,

1166
01:06:42,820 --> 01:06:45,500
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: identifying all those items that I've mentioned, Mr. Speaker,

1167
01:06:45,640 --> 01:06:50,960
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: is that based on the trajectory and based on the data that the Department of Finance has,

1168
01:06:51,100 --> 01:06:55,680
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: we are still on good track and on good financial condition, Mr. Speaker.

1169
01:06:55,900 --> 01:07:02,060
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Even, even if we pursue this reform tax packages, Mr. Speaker, Your Honors.

1170
01:07:02,060 --> 01:07:05,180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor.

1171
01:07:05,780 --> 01:07:10,320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Naiintindihan po natin ang kalagayan ng DOF, kalagayan ng bansa natin ngayon.

1172
01:07:10,740 --> 01:07:18,880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Pero hindi nyo rin po kasi maiaalis ang pangamba sa lahat tungkol dito sa tumataas at lumalalang utang ng bansa.

1173
01:07:19,720 --> 01:07:25,060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Pwede po ba tayo na ma-assure ng DOF sa ngayon that the current debt trajectory,

1174
01:07:25,900 --> 01:07:34,440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: will not compromise long-term fiscal sustainability and intergenerational security?

1175
01:07:34,440 --> 01:07:34,880
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Yes.

1176
01:07:34,880 --> 01:07:35,540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And equity?

1177
01:07:35,800 --> 01:07:40,600
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Yes, Mrs. Speaker. In fact, one of the reasons why we are mentioning also the benchmark,

1178
01:07:40,740 --> 01:07:49,560
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: the 70% international benchmark, is that we are low, low below the benchmark wherein dapat tayo ay mag-worry.

1179
01:07:49,940 --> 01:07:53,560
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: In fact, kung titignan po natin ang ating gross borrowing rate,

1180
01:07:54,320 --> 01:07:55,560
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: mas malaki po yung mga

1181
01:07:55,900 --> 01:08:02,760
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Progressive na bansa tulad ng Japan, United States of America, mas mataas po yung kanilang gross borrowing.

1182
01:08:03,120 --> 01:08:04,840
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Bibigyan ko lang po kayo ng data.

1183
01:08:06,040 --> 01:08:12,320
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Based on the debt levels po, Mr. Speaker, Your Honor, ng ating bansa, as compared with the other ASEAN countries.

1184
01:08:13,480 --> 01:08:21,720
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: In the ASEAN countries, Mr. Speaker, Malaysia, Thailand, Laos,

1185
01:08:21,720 --> 01:08:25,720
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: have projected a much, much bigger debt.

1186
01:08:25,900 --> 01:08:32,780
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: In terms of the 70% baseline benchmark po ng International Monetary Fund.

1187
01:08:33,260 --> 01:08:39,040
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: To say, for example, that there will be a trouble in terms of fiscal sustainability or debt sustainability.

1188
01:08:39,340 --> 01:08:40,820
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Sa Pilipinas po, way, way below.

1189
01:08:41,000 --> 01:08:47,880
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Again, I've mentioned earlier, 56.8% lang po yung ating debt to GDP.

1190
01:08:47,880 --> 01:08:54,340
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: And based on the prudent fiscal management that we have, as we have already until today itemized,

1191
01:08:54,740 --> 01:08:55,880
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: total tax reform packages.

1192
01:08:55,920 --> 01:08:58,400
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: It would even go lower, no?

1193
01:08:58,620 --> 01:09:02,680
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: It would even go lower in the coming years, no?

1194
01:09:02,900 --> 01:09:07,980
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: We anticipate that in the next year, it will be down to 56.1%.

1195
01:09:07,980 --> 01:09:16,960
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: So, basically, if we do reference, use the reference of the International Monetary Rate as our basis

1196
01:09:16,960 --> 01:09:23,280
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: to either say that we are now in deep trouble or we are okay or healthy in our financial standing,

1197
01:09:23,280 --> 01:09:25,880
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: I think the number would not lie.

1198
01:09:25,900 --> 01:09:42,680
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: 56.8% is way, way below the 70% benchmark on the International Monetary Rate na sinasabi po nilang medyo may problema doon.

1199
01:09:43,260 --> 01:09:45,780
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: So, medyo mababa po yung ating rate doon.

1200
01:09:46,620 --> 01:09:54,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, ibig sabihin po, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor, wala po dapat ipangamba ang taong bayan.

1201
01:09:54,100 --> 01:09:55,800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Hindi po tayo dapat.

1202
01:09:55,900 --> 01:09:57,360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mag-alala sa utang natin.

1203
01:09:57,360 --> 01:09:58,140
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Yes, Mrs. Speaker.

1204
01:09:58,760 --> 01:10:03,880
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: We can confidently say that dapat huwag tayo mangamba dahil unang-una.

1205
01:10:04,060 --> 01:10:06,540
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Again, let me reiterate because we're talking about borrowing.

1206
01:10:06,760 --> 01:10:09,240
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: We're also talking about our gross borrowing.

1207
01:10:09,740 --> 01:10:16,160
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Sinasabi po natin na hindi po tayo mapagamba kasi very less po yung possibility that we will also be affected

1208
01:10:16,160 --> 01:10:25,180
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: by international shocks or the fluctuating monetary rates kasi ang borrowing pala talaga natin are mostly our gross domestic borrowing,

1209
01:10:25,180 --> 01:10:25,780
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Mrs. Speaker.

1210
01:10:25,900 --> 01:10:33,460
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: At sinasabi po natin, ang ating nagiging baseline is yung 70% po na threshold na binigay po ng World Bank na sinabi po ng World Bank

1211
01:10:33,460 --> 01:10:39,180
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: na para ma-determine whether the sustainable yung debt levels ng ating bansa.

1212
01:10:39,360 --> 01:10:42,840
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Again, I've already given, Mr. Speaker, your honors, the numbers.

1213
01:10:44,200 --> 01:10:45,960
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Mrs. Speaker, your honors.

1214
01:10:45,960 --> 01:10:55,360
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: That is why with 58.6%, no, ang ating, ang ating, ang ating, ano, debt, no,

1215
01:10:55,900 --> 01:10:58,580
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: debt to GDP, Mrs. Speaker, ay medyo mababa.

1216
01:10:59,100 --> 01:11:03,960
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Iyon po yung rason, Mrs. Speaker, na marami pong pumapasok sa atin ng mga investors.

1217
01:11:04,400 --> 01:11:07,680
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: We have, because we have a very good investment ratings, no.

1218
01:11:08,060 --> 01:11:16,660
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: In fact, the best rating agencies also come out with that study na among many countries, as I've cited to you,

1219
01:11:16,660 --> 01:11:25,520
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: just to specifically give you an example, sa ASEAN, we are the lowest, no, ng rate na sinabi po ng,

1220
01:11:25,900 --> 01:11:26,900
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: ating data.

1221
01:11:27,440 --> 01:11:30,800
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: At the same time, mataas po ang ating credit rating.

1222
01:11:30,920 --> 01:11:35,060
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: That's why many investors do have confidence to put up their money in this country, Mrs. Speaker.

1223
01:11:35,180 --> 01:11:39,880
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: So, yes, to give you a short answer, we are confident and we are, we can manage over the years.

1224
01:11:40,360 --> 01:11:43,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor, sa inyong kasagutan.

1225
01:11:44,900 --> 01:11:55,020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sa punto po kasing ito, nilalatag natin ang lahat ng mga numero, pero ang akin lang pong isang, maibahagi ko lang po,

1226
01:11:55,900 --> 01:12:01,840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa, hindi po ako ekonomista, gusto ko pong unawain ang kalagayan ng ating bansa,

1227
01:12:02,360 --> 01:12:08,500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: isa lang po ang naiintindihan ko sa puntong ito bilang mambabatas at sa experience ko bilang mambabatas,

1228
01:12:08,560 --> 01:12:16,380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: itong mga numero ito, hindi maintindihan kung ang ating, sa pagganap ng ating batas,

1229
01:12:16,560 --> 01:12:23,300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: tuwing-tugi tayo magpapasa ng batas, magiging unfunded mandate, kasi walang pera.

1230
01:12:24,020 --> 01:12:25,380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kapag po tayo ay,

1231
01:12:25,380 --> 01:12:40,240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kaya tuwing budget hearing, magre-request po tayo na taasan ng mga pondo para sa mga programa at proyektong tingin natin ay dapat naman talaga mabigyan ng mataas na pagpupondo.

1232
01:12:40,240 --> 01:12:58,500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Katulad po sa human capital development, paano po natin maiintindihan yung mga figures na yan na sinasabing manageable yan, sustainable, kaya hindi po masama ang mangutang, lalo na po kung inuutang natin will redound to the greater benefit of our people.

1233
01:12:58,500 --> 01:13:08,800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Pero ang nakakabahala lang po kasi tuwing-tuwing magbabudget hearing tayo, ang atin pong naririnig lagi, tight fiscal space.

1234
01:13:10,240 --> 01:13:17,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Hindi ko po alam kung default answer yan or excuse, pero tuwing-tuwi, tight fiscal space.

1235
01:13:18,460 --> 01:13:25,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ang tanong ko po, huling katanungan ko na lamang po, paano pa ho ba natin luluwagan ang fiscal space na ito?

1236
01:13:26,180 --> 01:13:34,780
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Mr. Speaker, Your Honors, marami pong posibleng kasagutan dyan, pero as far as the Department of Finance is concerned,

1237
01:13:35,320 --> 01:13:39,900
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: and its main task really is to source out,

1238
01:13:40,240 --> 01:13:51,080
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: revenue in order that we can finance capital investments, kung ano po yung mga gastusin ng ating bansa, of course, hindi po tayo matatapos sa 30 minutes kung tayo po iisa-isahin.

1239
01:13:51,360 --> 01:13:59,540
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Pero kaya nga po, meron po tayong prudent fiscal management para nata-target po natin kung ano yung paggagastusan ng ating bawat ehansya.

1240
01:14:00,020 --> 01:14:07,240
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Ay yun po ay binabangga po natin kung ano pong meron tayo as a relative, just to give you a straight answer, pareho tayo, hindi po rin ako ekonomista,

1241
01:14:07,740 --> 01:14:10,080
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: pero ang tinitingnan ko po ay paano yung nagiging...

1242
01:14:10,240 --> 01:14:13,980
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: nagiging returns itong mga services na ito sa ating mga kababayan.

1243
01:14:14,380 --> 01:14:18,860
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: So definitely, there are, should be, number one, a prudent fiscal planning.

1244
01:14:19,860 --> 01:14:25,780
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: The fiscal management will only expand if there are revenues that we collect,

1245
01:14:26,060 --> 01:14:32,380
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: not only from the tax revenue collection, but even the non-tax proceeds, the revenues.

1246
01:14:32,380 --> 01:14:39,620
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: So it's how we can actually generate local economy, generate more jobs,

1247
01:14:40,240 --> 01:14:50,840
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: and as well as to, you know, to get more revenue in order that we can actually expand the fiscal space.

1248
01:14:50,980 --> 01:14:57,520
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Kasi mag-expand lang po yan kung gaano rin po kalaki yung ating pera.

1249
01:14:57,920 --> 01:15:00,060
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Kaya babalikan ko po kasi I think the question...

1250
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:01,460
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: was premised on pangungutang.

1251
01:15:02,040 --> 01:15:04,880
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Kaya nga po, ang pangungutang hindi naman po talaga siya masama.

1252
01:15:05,580 --> 01:15:09,520
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: Kaya nga, dapat meron coupled with prudent fiscal planning

1253
01:15:09,520 --> 01:15:11,400
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: kasi yung pangungutang, mas maganda po yan

1254
01:15:11,400 --> 01:15:14,220
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: kung nagtitrigger po yan ng economic activity sa baba.

1255
01:15:14,380 --> 01:15:16,600
Rep. Ziaur-Rahman "Zia" Alonto Adiong: And you agree on me on this, Mr. Speaker, Your Honors.

1256
