Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Para sa mga job order.

9974
09:36:24,900 --> 09:36:27,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At contract of service sa gobyerno.

9975
09:36:27,920 --> 09:36:32,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pangapat, no to Pax Silica and US military presence on our soil.

9976
09:36:32,940 --> 09:36:40,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: We need an independent industrialization policy that builds our own industries and jobs.

9977
09:36:40,820 --> 09:36:49,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And an independent defense policy that serves Filipino interests, not foreign strategy.

9978
09:36:50,100 --> 09:36:52,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bilang pangwakas, Madam Speaker,

9979
09:36:52,940 --> 09:36:58,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: these demands are urgent and they must be met.

9980
09:36:58,940 --> 09:37:06,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: But even if every one of these demands were granted, they would not change the fundamental character of this budget.

9981
09:37:06,440 --> 09:37:11,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Debate on the budget is ultimately a debate on national policy.

9982
